# Astelli Reclaimer's X is the mana actually spent: cast for its warp cost {2}{W}, paid with Lion's Eye Diamond's three white
# mana, X is 3 (its ruling), not 5. Basalt Monolith (mana value 3) is exactly the boundary and is returned; the Door of Destinies
# (mana value 4) cannot be targeted, and nor can a Mountain (a land card) or a Lightning Bolt (not a permanent card). Sol Ring and the
# Diamond itself, in the graveyard too, are legal. At the beginning of the next end step the warped Astelli Reclaimer is exiled.

[Bot1 Deck]
Lion's Eye Diamond
Astelli Reclaimer
Basalt Monolith
Door of Destinies
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Sol Ring
Mountain x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Lion's Eye Diamond.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Astelli Reclaimer.Cast(Ability: Warp)
Bot1.Battlefield.Lion's Eye Diamond.Activate(Color: White)
! Bot1.Target(Door of Destinies)
! Bot1.Target(Mountain)
! Bot1.Target(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Target(Basalt Monolith)
Bot1.Pass
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Astelli Reclaimer; Basalt Monolith
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 5
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Exile = Astelli Reclaimer

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Basalt Monolith
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 5
